{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>Behold, I have refined you.</b> An allusion to the exile." "<b>And not with silver.</b> The meaning is: and not with the refining of silver, to remove the dross, and they are the wicked." "<b>I have chosen you.</b> Some say it is like 'I have tested you' (בחנתיך), and it is not objectionable. But the correct interpretation is that it is as its literal meaning: 'I have chosen for you a furnace of affliction,' not the refining of silver."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 48, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:58:32.637400323Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}